From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 15:45:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pan/bi: lower ballot without WMASK on limited-CLPER GPUs

Every Vulkan subgroup shader that uses ballot (subgroupBallot,
subgroupElect, subgroupAny/All, read_first_invocation and the
subgroup*barrier CTS cases, which all go through ballot) faults the
Mali-G31 (Bifrost v7.0) with "js fault, status=INSTR_INVALID_ENC" at
the first clause holding WMASK.subgroup4. Probe shaders on the board
isolate it: plain stores, workgroup atomics, subgroup ids and
CLPER_OLD broadcasts run fine, every probe with a WMASK faults, for
1x1x1, 4x1x1 and 3x5x7 workgroups alike. G71/G72/G31 have only the old
CLPER form (BIFROST_LIMITED_CLPER) and evidently no WMASK either.

The subgroup is 4 lanes on those GPUs, so build the mask from four
CLPER_OLD reads of the predicate (lanes 0-3; an inactive source lane
reads as zero) masked with the lane bit and ORed together. 32-bit
booleans are 0/~0 in the IR, so the AND gives the bit directly.

Host dumps (panfrost drm-shim, PAN_GPU_ID=7093) of the probe shaders and
of dEQP-VK.subgroups.{basic,ballot_broadcast,clustered,vote,ballot_other}
cases: no WMASK left, CLPER_OLD only. Other GPUs are unchanged.

Generated-by: LLM
---
 .../compiler/bifrost/bifrost_compile.c        | 26 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bifrost_compile.c b/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bifrost_compile.c
index 2a318c6c293..96267e043b5 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bifrost_compile.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bifrost_compile.c
@@ -2067,6 +2067,32 @@ bi_emit_intrinsic(bi_builder *b, nir_intrinsic_instr *instr)
    case nir_intrinsic_ballot:
    case nir_intrinsic_ballot_relaxed: {
       assert(instr->src[0].ssa->bit_size == 32);
+
+      /* G71/G72/G31 (BIFROST_LIMITED_CLPER) have no WMASK: it faults them
+       * with INSTR_INVALID_ENC, like the full CLPER encoding. Their subgroup
+       * is 4 lanes, so gather the predicate of each lane with CLPER_OLD
+       * (which returns zero for an inactive source lane) and assemble the
+       * mask. 32-bit booleans are 0/~0, so AND with the lane bit. */
+      if (b->shader->quirks & BIFROST_LIMITED_CLPER) {
+         assert(pan_subgroup_size_gpu(b->shader->inputs->gpu_id) == 4);
+         bi_index pred = bi_src_index(&instr->src[0]);
+         bi_index mask = bi_null();
+
+         for (unsigned lane = 0; lane < 4; ++lane) {
+            bi_index v = bi_clper_old_i32(b, pred, bi_imm_u32(lane));
+            bi_index bit = bi_lshift_and_i32(b, v, bi_imm_u32(1 << lane),
+                                             bi_imm_u8(0));
+
+            if (lane == 3)
+               bi_lshift_or_i32_to(b, dst, mask, bit, bi_imm_u8(0));
+            else if (lane == 0)
+               mask = bit;
+            else
+               mask = bi_lshift_or_i32(b, mask, bit, bi_imm_u8(0));
+         }
+         break;
+      }
+
       enum bi_subgroup subgroup =
          bi_subgroup_from_cluster_size(pan_subgroup_size_gpu(b->shader->inputs->gpu_id));
       bi_wmask_to(b, dst, bi_src_index(&instr->src[0]), subgroup, 0);
